  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** KLXE experienced broad-based sequential declines across product lines in Q1, with only tech services and accommodations holding flat, and overall activity landing at the low end of expectations. However, the Northeast/Mid-Con segment showed notable year-over-year strength, with significant revenue growth and margin expansion, pointing to geographic pockets of resilience. Management characterized the quarter as the likely trough, signaling that demand headwinds in most service lines could be bottoming. The external environment for onshore oilfield services remains mixed, with some areas stabilizing while others face persistent pressure.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership has actively reduced the cost structure, reflected in meaningfully lower SG&A from ongoing efficiency measures, and emphasized that the Q1 performance marks an inflection point. The tone on the earnings call was that results are now poised to improve, and management is focusing on segment-level profitability gains, particularly in the Northeast/Mid-Con. With liquidity modest and the company still loss-making, capital allocation remains conservative. The narrative from management is one of disciplined execution through a cycle trough, with an expectation of a sequential recovery ahead.",
